#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A circuit with a Hadamard gate is made as follows:\n"
msgstr "Obwód kwantowy z bramką Hadamarda tworzy się następująco:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/bells-inequality-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/b9da36f3-3ccc-4af0-ae16-a1ce8741211a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/bells-inequality-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/b9da36f3-3ccc-4af0-ae16-a1ce8741211a-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"CNOT Controlled-NOT gate: This gate uses two qubits: a control and a target. Checks the state of a control qubit which is not changed. But if the control qubit is in the state $|1\\rangle$, the gate changes the state of the target qubit; if the state of the control qubit is $|0\\rangle$ no change is made at all. In the notation below, assume the first qubit is the control, and the second is the target.\n"
"$$\n"
"CNOT|00\\rangle = |00\\rangle, \\\\\n"
"CNOT|01\\rangle = |01\\rangle \\\\\n"
"CNOT|10\\rangle = |11\\rangle \\\\\n"
"CNOT|11\\rangle = |10\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Bramka CNOT (Controlled-NOT): Ta bramka używa dwóch kubitów: kontrolnego i docelowego. Sprawdza stan kubita kontrolnego, który nie jest zmieniany. Jeśli jednak kubit kontrolny jest w stanie $|1\\rangle$, bramka zmienia stan kubita docelowego; jeśli kubit kontrolny jest w stanie $|0\\rangle$, żadna zmiana nie jest dokonywana. W poniższej notacji przyjmijmy, że pierwszy kubit jest kontrolnym, a drugi docelowym.\n"
"$$\n"
"CNOT|00\\rangle = |00\\rangle, \\\\\n"
"CNOT|01\\rangle = |01\\rangle \\\\\n"
"CNOT|10\\rangle = |11\\rangle \\\\\n"
"CNOT|11\\rangle = |10\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

